# Commit Approved Code

- When the user has approved code changes, commit them before considering the task complete.
- After a successful commit, push the approved commit to the tracked remote branch unless the user asks not to push.
- Review the current git status and diff first so only approved changes are included.
- If unrelated or unapproved local changes are present, pause and ask how to proceed before committing.
